docs {
  # GET /api/artworks/orders/:slug/ — Order summary for the success page

  Returns the order summary shown on `/compra-exitosa/?order={slug}`.
  Public endpoint, no `Authorization` header. Throttled: `artwork_orders`
  60/hour (`429` when exceeded — wait and retry).

  Slug handoff: `POST buy` returns only `{checkout_url}` — the order slug
  is NOT in the buy response. Copy it from the Stripe success redirect
  (`{PUBLIC_SITE_URL}/compra-exitosa/?order={slug}`), then replace
  `0123456789ab` below with the real slug and Send. First line of action:
  replace the slug, then Send (the fake-hex placeholder never returns 200).

  `200` for orders in `paid_pending_data`, `data_complete`, `shipped`,
  `delivered`. `404` for unknown slugs, `cancelled`/`refunded` orders, or
  still-unpaid `pending_payment` (webhook not arrived yet → poll: every 3s,
  up to ~60s; stop on `200` or on repeated non-404 errors). If the redirect
  beats the webhook, the endpoint verifies via `retrieve_checkout_session`
  and applies the paid-transition itself.

  ## Status codes

  - `200 OK` — order summary
  - `404 Not Found` — unknown slug, `cancelled`/`refunded`, or unpaid `pending_payment` (poll/retry)
  - `429 Too Many Requests` — throttled (60 orders/hour)

  ## Response (200)

  ```json
  {
    "slug": "0123456789ab",
    "status": "paid_pending_data",
    "currency": "mxn",
    "amount": 15000.0,
    "paid_at": "2026-09-17T12:00:00Z",
    "artwork_title": "La columna rota",
    "artwork_image": "https://enredarte-dashboard.localhost/media/artworks/columna.webp",
    "artist_name": "Frida Kahlo"
  }
  ```

  8 fields: `slug`, `status`, `currency`, `amount` (number),
  `paid_at`, `artwork_title`, `artwork_image` (url|null), `artist_name`.

  ## Error (404)

  ```json
  {
    "status": "error",
    "message": "Not found.",
    "data": {}
  }
  ```
}
